comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T12:13:36.253Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched all statuses for GH-739, existing duplicate clusters, findDuplicateClusters CLI, and batch duplicate sweep. Closed pm-2i12ti supplies the batch primitive, pm-4ri6 covers create-time advice, and pm-jmld covers merge execution; none exposes the requested read workflow, so this is the canonical surface child."
  "2026-07-26T19:42:55.554Z","harness:codex","Evidence: shipped bounded all-status duplicate discovery through CLI, MCP action contracts, PmClient, and top-level SDK helpers. Results provide deterministic canonical IDs, compact similarity summaries, cluster limits/status/since filters, and safe close guidance. Completion/contracts snapshots and a real temporary-tracker integration test are included. Fresh installed CLI acceptance found one two-item cluster. Linked tests passed; full coverage and static gates are green."
  "2026-07-26T19:51:34.195Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: completed implementation is published in broad SDK delivery PR #753 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/753. Hosted checks and the exact-head AI review loop will be recorded after completion."
  "2026-07-26T20:16:28.290Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up: CodeRabbit identified two valid integration gaps on PR #753 exact head 55635b06: scalar MCP status/string limits were discarded, and duplicates action availability did not resolve its real CLI command path. Reopened and claimed solely for these active fixes; focused regression tests and regenerated contracts will accompany the implementation."
  "2026-07-26T20:18:20.726Z","harness:codex","Contract rationale: adding duplicates to PM_CORE_COMMAND_NAMES intentionally widens the exported readonly command tuple so SDK consumers, extension command reservation, and action availability match the already-shipped CLI. The SDK snapshot classifies any tuple signature change as breaking; this additive correction is explicitly acknowledged and regenerated."
  "2026-07-26T20:26:24.410Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: MCP duplicates now preserves scalar status strings, parses numeric string limits through the shared integer validator while retaining the documented default sentinel, and PM_CORE_COMMAND_NAMES now truthfully exposes the real duplicates command. Generated contracts report command_path=duplicates and cli_exposed=true. Both linked test bundles passed; focused 191/191 and 174/174 regressions passed; full repository coverage passed 375 files and 6425 tests at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; full lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static quality, 100% docstrings, package boundary, token budgets, SDK surface, import-cost, and transport-floor gates."
  "2026-07-26T20:35:41.774Z","harness:codex","Review implementation: duplicates --status now declares both repeatable and list semantics for contract-driven accumulation, and zsh uses the repeatable * option prefix so subsequent lifecycle filters remain discoverable. The regenerated full contract retains the earlier CLI exposure correction."
  "2026-07-26T20:53:25.294Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: repo-wide coverage passed 375 test files and 6,428 tests at exact 100% statements (44,307/44,307), branches (31,445/31,445), functions (9,061/9,061), and lines (43,046/43,046). Full lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static quality, 100% docstrings, package boundary, token budgets, SDK surface, import-cost, and transport-floor gates. Security scan and pnpm audit reported no secrets or vulnerabilities; packed npx acceptance passed all 15 bundled packages."
